{{also|Luke|lûke|lǚkè}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|luke}}, {{m|enm|leuk}}, {{m|enm|leuke}}, {{m|enm|lewke|t=lukewarm, tepid}}, perhaps from {{inh|en|ang|*hlēoc}}, a suffixed variant of {{der|en|ang|hlēow|t=warm}}. For the suffix, compare also the pairs {{noncog|ang|rēoc}} & {{m|ang|rēow}}; {{m|ang|slēac}} & {{m|ang|unslēaw|(un)slēaw}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/luːk/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|uːk|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|British|archaic}} [[lukewarm]]
#* '''1836''', Charles Dickens, ''The Pickwick Papers''
#*: Let me have nine penn'orth o' brandy and water '''luke''', and the inkstand, will you, miss?

